TI  - Seven new metabolites of drostanolone heptanoate by using Beauveria bassiana, and Macrophomina phaseolina cell suspension cultures.
PG  - 451-460
LID - 10.1039/c9ra05878h [doi]
AB  - The present study reports the biotransformation of an anabolic-androgenic steroid (AAS) drostanolone heptanoate (1) by using two microbial cultures, Beauveria bassiana, and Macrophomina phaseolina. Fermentation of 1 with B. bassiana yielded five new transformed products 2-6, while with M. phaseolina it afforded two new 7-8, and two known 9-10 metabolites. The main sites of hydroxylation in the steroidal skeleton of 1 were at C-5, C-7, C-11, C-14, C-15, and C-20, hydrolysis of the ester moiety at C-17, and reduction of the carbonyl group at C-3. The structures of the transformed products were determined by using mass, NMR, and other spectroscopic techniques.
