TI  - Antifeedant and antiphytopathogenic metabolites from co-culture of endophyte Irpex lacteus, phytopathogen Nigrospora oryzae, and entomopathogen Beauveria bassiana.
PG  - 104781
LID - S0367-326X(20)30363-4 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.fitote.2020.104781 [doi]
AB  - Five new tremulane sesquiterpenoids were isolated from co-culture of endophyte Irpex lacteus, phytopathogen Nigrospora oryzae, and entomopathogen Beauveria bassiana. All compounds showed obvious antifeedant activities against silkworm with inhibition percentages of 73-99%, at concentrations of 50 g/cm(2). Compound 11 indicated notable antifeedant activity with inhibition percentage of 93% at concentration of 6.25 g/cm(2) among them. Compounds 2, 3, 4, 8, 9, 15 and 16 indicated anti-fungal activities against I. lacteus with MIC values 8 g/mL, compounds 11, 12, 16-18 showed significant anti-fungal activity against N. oryzae with MICs 4 g/mL, and compounds 2, 5, 12 and 18 indicated significant anti-fungal activity against B. bassiana with MICs 8 g/mL. In addition, the I. lacteus should unite B. bassiana to inhibit the production of phytotoxins from N. oryzae in the ternary culture.
